Perun
Copyright 2026 lazyeel (https://github.com/lazyeel)

This product compiles and links the following software developed by lazyeel:
- Native binary projection runtime: PE32+ (Win32) and Mach-O x86_64
  (Darwin) image loading, relocation, import binding (perun-core)
- Guest API translation shims: Win32 to POSIX and macOS libSystem/Mach
  to Linux, including the FairPlay SAP session runtime (perun-shims)
- Command-line runner, image inspector, FairPlay SAP session driver, and
  the App Store client (perun-cli)

This product contains third-party open source software in object form,
under its own license:

- libc 0.2.189 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — The Rust Project — https://github.com/rust-lang/libc
- linkme, linkme-impl 0.3.37 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — David Tolnay — https://github.com/dtolnay/linkme
- bzip2-rs 0.1.2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — Paolo Barbolini — https://github.com/paolobarbolini/bzip2-rs
- crc32fast 1.5.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — Sam Rijs (srijs), Alex Crichton — https://github.com/srijs/rust-crc32fast
- cfg-if 1.0.4 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — Alex Crichton — https://github.com/rust-lang/cfg-if
- tinyvec 1.13.2 (Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT) — Lokathor — https://github.com/Lokathor/tinyvec

Crates used only to build the macro machinery (proc-macro2, quote, syn, unicode-ident) do not reach the distributed object form and are therefore not listed above.
linkme-impl is a proc macro, but the code it generates is compiled into the binaries, so it is listed.
